# Lotus CMS

Specialized knowledge for working with the Lotus Graph content management system.

## CMS Overview

**Type:** File-based CMS using Markdown with YAML frontmatter

**Location:** `src/content/*.md`

**Philosophy:** Content as code - version controlled, human-readable, editor-agnostic

**Compatibility:** Obsidian-compatible (can edit in Obsidian or any text editor)

## Graph Structure

### The Lotus Metaphor

The navigation system is inspired by a blooming lotus flower:
- **Center:** Current node (you are here)
- **Petals:** Child nodes (up to 8)
- **Bloom:** Navigate to a child (new center)
- **Return:** Navigate back to parent

### Hierarchy Rules

**Root:**
- ID: `home`
- No parent
- Entry point for all navigation

**Children:**
- Every node (except home) has a parent
- Parent must exist (no orphaned nodes)
- Maximum 8 children displayed per node

**Depth:**
- Unlimited nesting supported
- Recommended: 3-4 levels for UX
- Example: `home → lectures → lectures-neuroplasticity`

## Frontmatter Schema

### Required Fields

```yaml
---
id: unique-node-id
parent: parent-node-id
title_en: English Title
title_ru: Русский Заголовок
type: content
date: 2024.03.20
---
```

### Optional Fields

```yaml
tags: [tag1, tag2]
order: 1
image: /images/custom-cover.jpg
media: /videos/demo.mp4
```

### Field Reference

**id** (required)
- Unique identifier
- Format: kebab-case (lowercase, hyphens)
- Used in URLs: `?id=node-id`
- Examples: `lectures-neuroplasticity`, `events-pleinair`

**parent** (required)
- ID of parent node
- Must be `home` or existing node ID
- Defines position in hierarchy
- Example: `parent: lectures`

**title_en** (required)
- English title
- Keep concise (2-5 words ideal)
- Used in grid cells, breadcrumbs, sidebar
- Example: `Neuroplasticity and Art`

**title_ru** (required)
- Russian title
- Translation of title_en
- Keep semantic equivalence
- Example: `Нейропластичность и искусство`

**type** (required)
- Node behavior type
- Values: `hub`, `content`, `media`, `action`
- See "Node Types" section below

**date** (required)
- Last modified date
- Format: YYYY.MM.DD (dots, not dashes)
- Example: `2024.03.20`
- Can be synced with `npm run dates:sync`

**tags** (optional)
- Array of keywords
- Lowercase, English
- Used for search/categorization
- Displayed in footer
- Example: `[neuroscience, art, interactive]`

**order** (optional)
- Sort position in parent's grid
- Range: 0-8
- Lower numbers appear first
- If omitted, uses order of mention in parent's content

**image** (optional)
- Custom cover image path
- Overrides procedurally generated SVG
- Path relative to `public/`
- Example: `/images/content/custom-cover.jpg`

**media** (optional)
- Direct media URL for media nodes
- Video, audio, or image
- Example: `/videos/demo.mp4`

## Node Types

### hub - Container Node

**Purpose:** Navigation folder that displays children

**Behavior:**
- Shows children in Lotus Grid (3x3)
- Center cell: current hub
- Surrounding cells: children (max 8)
- Click child to navigate

**Icon:** Layers

**Example:**
```yaml
---
id: lectures
parent: home
title_en: Lectures
title_ru: Лекции
type: hub
tags: [education, talks]
date: 2024.03.20
---

## Lectures

A collection of talks and presentations exploring the intersection of neuroscience, art, and consciousness.

---RU---

## Лекции

Коллекция выступлений и презентаций, исследующих пересечение нейронауки, искусства и сознания.
```

### content - Article Node

**Purpose:** Text content page

**Behavior:**
- Displays text in reading panel
- Can include images, videos (embedded)
- Supports markdown formatting
- Can have children (displayed in grid)

**Icon:** FileText

**Example:**
```yaml
---
id: lectures-neuroplasticity
parent: lectures
title_en: Neuroplasticity and Art
title_ru: Нейропластичность и искусство
type: content
tags: [neuroscience, brain, art]
date: 2024.03.20
order: 1
---

## How Art Shapes the Brain

Neuroplasticity is the brain's ability to reorganize itself...

---RU---

## Как искусство формирует мозг

Нейропластичность — это способность мозга реорганизовывать себя...
```

### media - Media Node

**Purpose:** Full-screen media display

**Behavior:**
- Opens lightbox immediately
- No text panel
- Supports video, audio, images
- Can have poster/thumbnail

**Icon:** Film / Image / AudioLines (based on media type)

**Example:**
```yaml
---
id: demo-video
parent: works
title_en: Demo Video
title_ru: Демо Видео
type: media
tags: [video, demo]
date: 2024.03.20
---

![[https://example.com/demo.mp4 | Demo Video | /images/covers/demo.jpg]]
```

### action - Action Node

**Purpose:** External link or special action

**Behavior:**
- Executes action on click
- Opens external URL
- Triggers email client
- No children

**Icon:** Zap

**Example:**
```yaml
---
id: contact-email
parent: contacts
title_en: Email Us
title_ru: Напишите нам
type: action
tags: [contact]
date: 2024.03.20
---

mailto:hello@odadream.art
```

## Content Format

### Bilingual Structure

**Template:**
```markdown
---
[frontmatter]
---

## English Heading

English content here...

You can use:
- **Bold** and *italic*
- [Links](https://example.com)
- Lists
- Images: ![alt](/path/to/image.jpg)
- Code blocks

---RU---

## Русский Заголовок

Русский контент здесь...

Вы можете использовать:
- **Жирный** и *курсив*
- [Ссылки](https://example.com)
- Списки
- Изображения: ![alt](/path/to/image.jpg)
- Блоки кода
```

**Critical:** The separator `---RU---` MUST be present to split EN/RU content.

### Markdown Support

**Supported:**
- Headings (##, ###, ####)
- Bold, italic, strikethrough
- Lists (ordered, unordered)
- Links
- Images
- Code blocks
- Blockquotes
- Tables (via remark-gfm)

**Not Supported:**
- HTML tags (sanitized)
- Scripts
- Iframes (use wiki-link syntax instead)

## Media Embedding

### Standard Markdown Images

```markdown
![Alt text](/images/content/photo.jpg)
```

**Use for:**
- Static images
- Simple embedding
- When no custom poster needed

### Wiki-Link Syntax

**Format:** `![[url | title | poster]]`

**Simple:**
```markdown
![[https://example.com/video.mp4]]
```

**With Title:**
```markdown
![[https://example.com/video.mp4 | My Video]]
```

**With Title and Poster:**
```markdown
![[https://example.com/video.mp4 | My Video | /images/covers/video-poster.jpg]]
```

**Use for:**
- Videos with custom thumbnails
- Audio with cover art
- External media URLs
- Advanced media control

### Media Types

**Video:**
- Formats: `.mp4`, `.webm`, `.mov`
- Displays as video player in lightbox
- Supports poster images

**Audio:**
- Formats: `.mp3`, `.wav`, `.ogg`
- Displays as audio player
- Supports cover art

**Images:**
- Formats: `.jpg`, `.png`, `.gif`, `.webp`
- Displays in lightbox
- Supports zoom/pan

## Grid Sorting

### Sort Modes

**Configuration:** `src/constants.ts` → `LOTUS_SORT_MODE`

**by-mention** (current):
1. Structural children (by `order` field)
2. Embedded nodes + media (by order of mention in text)

**by-type** (alternative):
1. Structural children (by `order` field)
2. Embedded nodes (by `order` field)
3. Media files (by order of mention)

### Order Field

**Purpose:** Control display sequence in grid

**Range:** 0-8 (matches grid limit)

**Behavior:**
- Lower numbers appear first
- If omitted, uses default ordering
- Only affects nodes with same parent

**Example:**
```yaml
# lectures-intro.md
order: 0  # Appears first

# lectures-advanced.md
order: 1  # Appears second

# lectures-expert.md
order: 2  # Appears third
```

## Embedded Nodes

### Wiki-Link for Nodes

You can embed other nodes in content using wiki-link syntax:

```markdown
Check out our [[lectures]] section for more information.

Specifically, see [[lectures-neuroplasticity|this lecture on neuroplasticity]].
```

**Behavior:**
- Embedded nodes appear in Lotus Grid
- Sorted according to `LOTUS_SORT_MODE`
- Marked with `_isEmbedded: true` flag (runtime)

**Use Cases:**
- Cross-references between content
- Featured content
- Related articles
- Dynamic grid composition

## Asset Management

### Procedural SVG Backgrounds

**Automatic Generation:**
```bash
npm run assets:generate
```

**What it does:**
- Reads all node IDs from `src/content/*.md`
- Generates unique SVG for each node
- Uses seeded random (same ID = same output)
- Saves to `public/images/nodes/{id}.svg`

**Algorithm:**
- Vibrant Art Engine
- Cyberpunk/neon aesthetic
- Geometric primitives
- Noise textures
- Custom palettes

**When to run:**
- After creating new nodes
- After renaming nodes
- When regenerating visual style

### Custom Images

**Override procedural generation:**

```yaml
---
id: my-node
image: /images/content/custom-cover.jpg
---
```

**Image requirements:**
- Aspect ratio: 16:9 or 4:3
- Resolution: 1200x800 minimum
- Format: JPG, PNG, WebP
- Location: `public/images/content/`

## Content Validation

### Check for Orphaned Nodes

```bash
npm run assets:map
```

**Output:** `scripts/CONTENT_TREE.md`

**Shows:**
- Full content hierarchy
- Orphaned nodes (invalid parents)
- Media file references
- Node counts

**Example output:**
```
📊 CONTENT STATISTICS
Total Nodes: 84
Hubs: 12
Content: 68
Media: 3
Actions: 1

⚠️ ORPHANED NODES:
- broken-node (parent: non-existent)
```

### Validation Checklist

Before committing:

- [ ] Frontmatter is valid YAML
- [ ] All required fields present
- [ ] ID is unique
- [ ] Parent exists
- [ ] Bilingual content complete
- [ ] Separator `---RU---` present
- [ ] Media links are valid
- [ ] No orphaned nodes
- [ ] Assets generated

## Common Patterns

### Creating Hub with Children

**1. Create hub:**
```yaml
# new-hub.md
---
id: new-hub
parent: home
title_en: New Hub
title_ru: Новый Хаб
type: hub
---
```

**2. Create children:**
```yaml
# child1.md
---
id: child1
parent: new-hub  # References hub
title_en: Child 1
title_ru: Ребёнок 1
type: content
order: 0
---
```

**3. Generate assets:**
```bash
npm run assets:generate
```

### Adding Media Gallery

```markdown
## Gallery

![[/images/gallery/photo1.jpg]]
![[/images/gallery/photo2.jpg]]
![[/images/gallery/photo3.jpg]]
```

**Result:** 3 media nodes in grid

### Cross-Referencing Content

```markdown
## Related Content

For more information, see:
- [[lectures-neuroplasticity|Neuroplasticity lecture]]
- [[research-dashran|Dashran research]]
- [[events-pleinair|Pleinair event]]
```

**Result:** 3 embedded nodes in grid

### External Links

```markdown
## External Resources

- [Wikipedia](https://wikipedia.org)
- [Research Paper](https://doi.org/...)
```

**Result:** Standard markdown links (not nodes)

## Obsidian Integration

### Why Obsidian?

- Visual graph view
- Wiki-link support
- Markdown editor
- Tag management
- Search functionality

### Setup

1. Open `src/content/` folder in Obsidian
2. Obsidian detects `.obsidian/` config
3. Edit files in Obsidian
4. Changes sync via git

### Obsidian Features

**Graph View:**
- Visualize node connections
- See orphaned nodes
- Explore structure

**Wiki Links:**
- `[[node-id]]` syntax works
- Auto-completion
- Link preview

**Tags:**
- Tag pane shows all tags
- Click to filter
- Organize content

### Limitations

- Frontmatter editing is manual
- No bilingual preview
- No procedural SVG preview
- Must run `npm run assets:generate` separately

## Best Practices

### Content Writing

**Titles:**
- Concise (2-5 words)
- Descriptive
- Bilingual consistency

**Descriptions:**
- Clear and engaging
- Use active voice
- Break into paragraphs
- Include media where relevant

**Tags:**
- 2-5 tags per node
- Lowercase
- Consistent terminology
- English only

### Structure

**Hierarchy:**
- Logical grouping
- Consistent depth
- Clear parent-child relationships

**Grid Composition:**
- Max 8 children per hub
- Use `order` for important items
- Balance content types

**Cross-References:**
- Link related content
- Create discovery paths
- Avoid circular references

### Maintenance

**Regular Tasks:**
- Run `npm run assets:map` to check structure
- Validate no orphaned nodes
- Update dates (`npm run dates:sync`)
- Regenerate assets after changes

**Version Control:**
- Commit content changes
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Keep content and code separate

## Troubleshooting

### Orphaned Node

**Symptom:** Node doesn't appear in navigation

**Cause:** Invalid parent ID

**Fix:**
1. Run `npm run assets:map`
2. Find orphaned node in output
3. Update `parent` field to valid ID
4. Regenerate assets

### Missing Separator

**Symptom:** Russian content not displayed

**Cause:** Missing `---RU---` separator

**Fix:**
1. Open `.md` file
2. Add `---RU---` between EN and RU content
3. Save file

### Broken Media Link

**Symptom:** Media doesn't load

**Cause:** Invalid path or missing file

**Fix:**
1. Check file exists at path
2. Verify path starts with `/`
3. Check file extension
4. Regenerate assets

### Grid Overflow

**Symptom:** Warning in console about too many children

**Cause:** More than 8 children

**Fix:**
1. Reduce number of children
2. Create intermediate hubs
3. Use `order` to prioritize important items

## Integration with Scripts

### generate-assets.js

**Reads:**
- All `.md` files in `src/content/`
- Extracts node IDs
- Extracts media references

**Generates:**
- SVG backgrounds for nodes
- Fallback SVGs for media

### generate-map.js

**Reads:**
- All `.md` files
- Parses frontmatter
- Builds graph structure

**Outputs:**
- `scripts/CONTENT_TREE.md`
- Hierarchy visualization
- Orphaned node detection

### sync-dates.js

**Reads:**
- Git history for each `.md` file
- Last commit date

**Updates:**
- `date` field in frontmatter
- Syncs with git history

